# =============================================================================
# WASP Lynis profile
# =============================================================================
# Installed to /etc/lynis/custom.prf and picked up automatically.
#
# Every skip below is here because Lynis is auditing a general-purpose Linux
# server and this is not one. It is a single-purpose Alpine VM whose only job
# is to run three containers. Findings that would be real on a shared server
# are structurally impossible or already handled here.
#
# THE RULE FOR ADDING TO THIS FILE: a skip needs a reason that survives being
# read back in six months by someone who did not write it. "Noisy" is not a
# reason. If the honest justification is "we have not fixed it yet", it
# belongs in TODO.md as a known gap, not here as a suppression — a profile
# that hides real findings is worse than no profile, because the score then
# says the opposite of the truth.
#
# Review this whenever the VM's design changes. A skip that made sense for a
# container host makes no sense the day something else is installed.
# =============================================================================

# ── Partitioning ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lynis wants separate /home, /tmp, /var and /var/log partitions. This VM has
# one root filesystem by design: it is provisioned from a single qcow2 whose
# size is set at install and grown with qm resize. Multiple partitions would
# make that resize a manual, error-prone operation for no security gain here —
# the containers write to bind mounts under /home/wpuser/wp, and disk
# exhaustion is monitored rather than partitioned against.
skip-test=FILE-6310

# ── GRUB / bootloader ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Alpine on Proxmox boots via the hypervisor; there is no GRUB configuration
# to password-protect. The equivalent control is Proxmox access itself, which
# is out of scope for an audit run inside the guest.
skip-test=BOOT-5122

# ── Host web server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lynis looks for Apache/nginx configuration on the host and reports its
# absence or misconfiguration. Apache runs INSIDE the WordPress container and
# is hardened there (see payload/apache-conf). There is no host web server,
# and there should not be.
skip-test=HTTP-6622
skip-test=HTTP-6624
skip-test=HTTP-6626
skip-test=HTTP-6640
skip-test=HTTP-6641
skip-test=HTTP-6643

# ── Mail transfer agent ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No MTA listens on this VM. Outbound mail goes through an authenticated
# remote relay via msmtp and PHPMailer; nothing accepts mail inbound. Lynis
# reporting a missing or unconfigured MTA is correct and irrelevant.
skip-test=MAIL-8818

# ── Name services ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No local resolver or NIS. Container DNS is served by aardvark-dns on the
# podman bridge; the host uses the network's resolver.
skip-test=NAME-4028

# ── Time synchronisation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT skipped, deliberately. chrony matters here: TLS certificate validation
# and log correlation both depend on the clock, and the egress firewall opens
# 123/udp specifically for it. If Lynis reports a time problem, it is real.
# (Recorded so nobody adds a skip later "to clean up the report".)

# ── Package management ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lynis expects a package manager with signed-update tooling in a shape it
# recognises. Alpine's apk signs indexes and packages, and unattended upgrades
# run nightly from cron; the test does not detect this arrangement.
skip-test=PKGS-7398

# ── Containers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lynis's Docker tests assume a Docker daemon. This VM runs rootful Podman
# with no daemon, and container hardening is verified by
# validate-wordpress.sh: digest pinning, cap-drop, read-only mounts and the
# internal database network. The relevant assurance exists; Lynis simply
# cannot see it.
skip-test=CONT-8104
skip-test=CONT-8106

# ── Reporting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Machine-readable output for wp-hardening.sh to summarise.
show-report-solution=yes
quick=yes
